<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Girolamo Savonarola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1452–<a href="/years/1498">1498</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Girolamo Savonarola (1452–1498) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friar</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> who preached in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> from 1490, denouncing corruption in the church and the luxury of the Medici. After the expulsion of the Medici in 1494 he dominated the restored republic, promoting moral reform and the 'bonfires of the vanities'. Excommunicated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-alexander-vi">Pope Alexander VI</a> in 1497, he lost popular support and was hanged and burned in the Piazza della Signoria in 1498.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/girolamo-savonarola.jpg" alt="Girolamo Savonarola" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fra Bartolomeo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Savonarola_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
